# Talkwer visual contract

## Purpose

Guardrails for refactors where code quality changes are allowed but design changes
are not.

## Non-negotiables

- Keep existing visual identity: dark editorial palette, orange accent usage,
  type scale intent, and section order.
- Preserve existing spacing rhythm and layout width behavior (`pad-x`,
  `max-w-[1600px]`, section paddings).
- Preserve current animation intent and timing feel unless fixing accessibility
  via reduced-motion fallbacks.
- Do not swap template families (Talkwer and Voyager styles must stay separate).

## Allowed changes

- Move code, extract components, split files, and normalize data/types.
- Replace duplicated markup with reusable primitives when rendered output remains
  equivalent.
- Improve semantics/accessibility without changing the visual surface.

## Verification checklist

- Compare before/after class composition and section hierarchy.
- Confirm no new colors/typography scales introduced to active homepage.
- Validate that major above-the-fold and section CTA visuals remain unchanged.

